WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.650
An owner nominates a passkey for agent 30.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:06.650
It can pause the agent from a phone.
A P256 signature, checked by Monad’s precompile.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.950
The same passkey seals the agent’s runbook.
Where it runs, how to restart it, why it was stopped.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.850
Mera turns the passkey’s PRF output into a key,
AES-256-GCM, made in the browser and nowhere else.

5
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.350
The passkey opens it again.

6
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.750
Any device the passkey syncs to can read it.
Nobody else can, including us.

7
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:29.250
This is everything the chain holds.
A salt, a nonce and ciphertext. No key, no text.

8
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:37.050
One passkey, two keys.
One stops the agent. One opens its notes.

